<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds start a little easier.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds start a little easier.</headline>
<text>
<p>---------------------(Snapshot at 0750 GMT)---------------------</p>
<p>* DUTCH STATE LOANS	 PRICES			  BID YIELDS</p>
<p>  June 1999 7.50 pct	107.18/28 (-0.07)	   3.67 (unch)</p>
<p>  Feb  2002		   114.88/98 (-0.03)	   4.61 (unch)</p>
<p>  Feb  2007 5.75 pct	101.16/26 (-0.07)	   5.59 (+0.01)</p>
<p>  Jan  2023		   114.24/44 (-0.10)	   6.35 (+0.01)</p>
<p>* BUND FUTURE (Sept)	101.43 (+0.09)</p>
<p>  TREASURIES  (June)	112.5  (-0.03 vs pvs Dutch close)</p>
<p>* DM/NLG			1.1253 (prev 1.1247)</p>
<p>--------------------------(SPREADS)----------------------------</p>
<p>*DSLs versus Bunds  (pvs close)    *DSL curve     (pvs close)</p>
<p> 5 yr	 +0.01	+0.01	  10-2 yr  192     (194)</p>
<p> 10 yr	-0.13	-0.14	  10-5 yr   97	(98)</p>
<p> Long	 -0.16	-0.16</p>
<p>-------------------------(June 19)-----------------------------</p>
<p>* Dutch bonds start a little easier in quiet trade, volumes thin. Debt markets expected to drift near-term but prospect of an FOMC meeting on July 1 and 2 could increase volatility then. Dealers see some demand for near-term non-state paper.</p>
